course: dictionary
lesson: 13159
title: Formerly and the past
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Formerly» means in the past, before now, but not any more. Look at the clue words around it: «The park was formerly a rubbish tip, but now it has a lake.» The word tells you the tip is in the past, and the park is different today.
explain: Formerly shows change. You often find it with a word like «known» or «called», as in «formerly known as». Read the words around it and ask: what used to be true, and what is true now?
explain: In formal writing and on signs, formerly can replace «used to be». «The old barn, formerly a farm, is now our school hall.» To check, swap in «used to be»: «The old barn, used to be a farm, is now our school hall.» The meaning stays the same, so formerly does the same job.
fact: Formerly means in the past, but not any more.
fact: Formerly is an adverb, a word that tells you more about something, such as when it happened.
fact: Formerly is often used in formal writing and on signs.
fact: «Formerly called» gives the old name of a place or thing: «Ruby Street, formerly called Gold Road.»
fact: A quick check is to swap in «used to be»: if the sentence still makes sense, formerly means the same.
exercise: «The park was formerly a rubbish tip.» What does formerly mean? | Right now | Very quickly | *Before now, but not any more | In the future
exercise: «The shop, formerly called Corner Books, now sells toys.» What does formerly called tell you? | The shop will close soon | The shop is brand new | *The shop had an old name | The shop only ever sold books
exercise: «Mrs Lee, formerly our headteacher, now lives by the sea.» Which words could replace formerly? | *used to be | will be | always | very
test: «The old barn, formerly a farm, is now our school hall.» What does formerly show? | It has never been a farm | It is a farm today | It will be a farm next year | *It used to be a farm, but not now
test: «Dan, formerly a chef, now runs a bike shop.» Which phrase is the best swap for formerly? | *used to be | always | will become | quickly
exam: Which phrase means the same as «formerly known as»? | never called | still called | soon called | *once called
